System Architecture Specification
Version 0.1
Architecture Status: Foundational Implementation Architecture
Product: OneDraft
AI System: Aria Powered
Primary Function: AI-assisted architectural design and coordinated documentation
Primary Output: Model-derived architectural document sets

1. ARCHITECTURAL OBJECTIVE
OneDraft shall be implemented as a modular, model-driven software platform in which artificial intelligence, parametric geometry, regulatory intelligence, document generation and customer interaction operate as coordinated services around a persistent Project Model.
The system shall not depend upon a single AI response to generate an architectural project.
Instead, OneDraft shall maintain a persistent computational state.
The fundamental architecture is:
USER
→ APPLICATION
→ PROJECT ORCHESTRATOR
→ PROJECT MODEL
→ SPECIALIZED ENGINES
→ VALIDATION
→ DOCUMENT GENERATION
→ CUSTOMER REVIEW
→ REVISION
→ FINAL OUTPUT

2. SYSTEM LAYERS
OneDraft shall be divided into eight principal layers.
Layer 1 — Customer Experience
Layer 2 — Application/API Layer
Layer 3 — Aria Intelligence and Orchestration
Layer 4 — Project Model and Persistence
Layer 5 — Geometry / CAD / BIM Computation
Layer 6 — Regulatory and Validation Intelligence
Layer 7 — Rendering and Document Production
Layer 8 — Infrastructure / Security / Billing / Audit
Each layer shall have defined responsibilities.
No layer should unnecessarily become responsible for another layer's functions.

