48. THE FIRST MVP
The minimum viable OneDraft system should therefore accomplish one complete loop:
A user describes a building → OneDraft constructs a structured project → CAD-AI creates the model → drawings are generated → the user redlines the project → CAD-AI modifies the model → affected drawings regenerate → the user accepts the final revision → OneDraft produces the final document package.
If this loop works reliably, the fundamental product exists.
Everything else becomes expansion.

49. DEFINING DIFFERENTIATOR
OneDraft's principal technological differentiator is not simply that Aria can produce architectural drawings.
It is that:
THE AI, PROJECT MODEL, GEOMETRY, REGULATORY CONTROLS, DRAWINGS, REDLINES AND FINAL DOCUMENTATION ALL PARTICIPATE IN ONE VERSIONED SYSTEM.
That creates continuity between:
What the customer requested
What the AI interpreted
What the model contains
What the geometry represents
What the code engine evaluated
What the drawings depict
What changed
What was accepted
and:
What was ultimately exported.

